{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration","id":969924,"title":"Obtenebration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T08:18:59-07:00","id":969924,"title":"Obtenebration","content":"I guess some of you are familiar with Arms of the abyss (yeah those hentai shadow/darkness tentacles).<br /> I was wondering, it's possible to do that with Forces 3 , Life 3 and Prime 2, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:43:31-07:00","id":969942,"title":"","content":"No need for life. Prime and forces allows you to create a moving, dark area of kinetic energy that you control. Remember that the arms of the abyss don't act on their own either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:51:24-07:00","id":969948,"title":"","content":"Any idea what it's stats will be like, str or dex, health levels and such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:37:20-07:00","id":969988,"title":"","content":"Up to the ST judgement. There are no rules-as-written for such a specific thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:49:34-07:00","id":970034,"title":"","content":"One question is whether you're just trying to recreate the effect of having black tentacle things do your bidding, or if you want to actually summon them from the abyss in the same way Obtenebration does. For the former Prime and Forces should cut it, for the latter you might have to mix in something like Spirit or Entropy depending on how you fit the abyss into Mage cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:33:16-07:00","id":970168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=969942#post969942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No need for life. Prime and forces allows you to create a moving, dark area of kinetic energy that you control. Remember that the arms of the abyss don't act on their own either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Forces is that, just like with most of MtAs, it doesn't care what the scientific consensus says a force is. It depends on Paradigm. Some Mages believe that darkness is merely an absence of light (and that cold is an absence of heat). But others might believe that darkness is an opposing force to light (and cold an opposing force to heat). If your Mage believes that darkness has substance - exists in and of itself - then you can manipulate darkness in the same way as light.<br /> <br /> So yes, you can totally grab shadows and have them act like tentacles. Given sufficient ambient darkness, and you might not even need Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:46:18-07:00","id":970282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970168#post970168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, you can totally grab shadows and have them act like tentacles. Given sufficient ambient darkness, and you might not even need Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but you will have a hard time also giving them felt substance (in the form of kinetic energy). Now, what you *could* do without Prime (And it's up to paradigm as you said) is take the light in a tentacle shape, and transform it into kinetic energy instead - That would kill two birds with one stone. You'd get the darkness, and the felt substance in the form of kinetics. The question if the relatively small amount of energy/power mere light of that amount would have as kinetic energy is up to the ST, but..it probably wouldn't exactly be impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:55:39-07:00","id":970287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970282#post970282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, but you will have a hard time also giving them felt substance (in the form of kinetic energy). Now, what you *could* do without Prime (And it's up to paradigm as you said) is take the light in a tentacle shape, and transform it into kinetic energy instead - That would kill two birds with one stone. You'd get the darkness, and the felt substance in the form of kinetics. The question if the relatively small amount of energy/power mere light of that amount would have as kinetic energy is up to the ST, but..it probably wouldn't exactly be impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that if Forces can allow you to transform one force to another, it should also be able to endow one force with the <i>properties</i> of another. Wind that cuts, electricity that destroys vampire flesh like sunlight (ala Jojo's Bizarre Adventure), and even shadows that strike like concussive force. It's also the theory that underlies the idea of Hard Light holograms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:53:17-07:00","id":970538,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops you from manipulating shadow tentacles like that, but giving them stats like Obtenebration does and any combat prowess? That'd take a lot of successes, and immense preparation time, and yet that'd be like 1-3 tentacles.<br /> <br /> It's simply ineffective, I don't even see why would you want to do this when mage can do much better stuff in shorter time and with more efficiency. Doing what you said is just..<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, there's a hill. We can just walk over it OR we can go around the entire world and eventually appear on the other side&quot; - your case is the second one.<br /> <br /> But if you REALLY want to do that, then -<br /> <br /> You could materialize them the way Spirits are materialized. Spirits are materialized with Spirit 4 + Prime 4, where each success gives them +2 Health Levels (as per How do you DO that?) and stats can be given just like Life 3/4 does (though you don't need Life in this).<br /> <br /> Now, for those tentacles, that'd be Forces 4 + Prime 4. Forces 4 for manipulating patches of darkness to create tentacles, Prime 4 to materialize and you're good to go. (Keep in mind the immense amount of successes you will need + all the Paradox).<br /> <br /> Here's the trick though - they won't be independant. You'll have to be there and constantly manipulate them (did I mention you also need successes for Duration?). If you want to make them permament (that'd take way more successes), and give them your own mind with Mind 5 (even more successes), that'd be kind of very hard to pull off and will certainly take a long ritual.<br /> <br /> To sum it up: base difficulty of 4 (rank of Sphere, 5 if Mind 5 is used) + 4 (it's vulgar). +1 success per +2 Health levels for a /single/ tentacle. (example: 15 successes to give three tentacles 10 Health levels on each). +1 success per tentacle per Attribute that you want to increase, and +2 once it's 6 or more. (+45 successes if you want 3 tentacles to have 5 Strength, 5 Dexterity and 5 Stamina, each). From 5 to 10 successes to give each their own consciousness with Mind 5 so you don't have to be there (15-30 successes, otherwise they just stand moveless if you're away. In fact, once you leave - you lose control over them, unless you have Correspondence 4 to constantly maintain a distant link. Say hello to more successes).<br /> <br /> Oh and Duration! If you want them to last a decent while at least, I suggest investing another 4-5 successes, and 6+ if you want them to be there permamently.<br /> <br /> So let's see, in total that's.. 93 successes required to make tentacles with next stats: 3 tentacles, 10 Health Levels, 5 in all Physical Attributes, they have basic mind and they will stay there permamently. (No link though, else that's another +6 successes, aka +2 for each to link to yourself as per &quot;affecting something/ somebody else&quot;, if not more. So if anything happens, they're up to themselves to decide what to do with basic mindset of quite a silly person)<br /> <br /> Why so many successes? Here's the formula: 5 successes per tentacle for each to have 10 Health levels (5*3 = 15) + 15 successes per tentacle to have 5 in all Physical Attributes (15*3 = 45) + 5 successes per tentacle to give it basic mind (5*3 = 15) + 6 or more successes to make each permament (6*3 = 18), and up to you about link (another 6+ successes if you want to).<br /> That's 15 + 15 + 45 + 18 = 93.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that ritual lol.<br /> <br /> Sure you can do each tentacle separately and reduce successes, but still really long time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:39:47-07:00","id":970569,"title":"","content":"The general Mage problem: scaling successes.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense to demand 100 successes for 3 shadowthings, regardless what the rules say.<br /> They work for a certain range but start to get ridiculous very fast.<br /> <br /> By your reasoning you need around 50 successes for a fireball that kills a dozen people in an elevator (12 times 4 for 8 damage levels)<br /> <br /> 16 is already way to much IMO (4 damage +12 targets)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Example added 09-16-2016, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:49:45-07:00","id":970576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970569#post970569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general Mage problem: scaling successes.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense to demand 100 successes for 3 shadowthings, regardless what the rules say.<br /> They work for a certain range but start to get ridiculous very fast.<br /> <br /> By your reasoning you need around 50 successes for a fireball that kills a dozen people in an elevator (12 times 4 for 8 damage levels)<br /> <br /> 16 is already way to much IMO (4 damage +12 targets)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is not how it even works.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 is a single target. If you want to hit multiple people, sure you'll need more successes, because Forces 3 is /not supposed/ to hit many people. (But if you incinerate someone in the elevator, who says that fire will not spread onto others as mundane fire, and deal damage too?)<br /> <br /> If you use something like Forces 5 instead, then it's Area of Effect by default, and everyone you intended to hit (assuming they're not too far from each other) will be hit.<br /> <br /> Sphere ranks exist for a reason with their different power scales and purposes, and I also stated for a reason that there are much better methods to slay your foes or protect some area. In general, creating anything from scratch (and creating those shadow things = creating stuff from scratch) will take a lot of effort. You're just not meant to get-go use them in combat, Mage is all about preparation.<br /> <br /> Besides, in addition to what I just said, Mage can come out with better shadow tentacles (and with their own mind, and permament) than Lasombra would. If you want get-go abillities, Vampire or Werewolf fit more for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:58:57-07:00","id":970578,"title":"","content":"But 3 shadows should not take 3 times as much successes than 1 shadow, thats what additional targets are for.<br /> Chain-lighting is damage + targets not damage times targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:34:59-07:00","id":970584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970578#post970578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 3 shadows should not take 3 times as much successes than 1 shadow, thats what additional targets are for.<br /> Chain-lighting is damage + targets not damage times targets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I don't think I get your point here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, I got it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, but you have to materialize each shadow separately, that's the thing. Creating new stuff is just hard to do, that's how it works. Werewolves and Vampires can create stuff too, but it's mostly fragile, or temporary, or is flawed.<br /> <br /> Plus, you're giving them stats, that's also something.<br /> <br /> Why do you think Technocracy can't just create crapton of clones and send them to do all the battle stuff? Because it takes a lot of effort, expertise and time to create something new from scratch. Same story with HIT Marks.<br /> <br /> That's just how it's supposed to be. You aren't gonna go around and spawn things with ease, at least nothing strong or even permament or.. you got my point.<br /> <br /> You can, of course, tone it down and give each shadow some petty health, short life span and low stats, and all of the successes requirements will drastically fall. But is it worth it? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> There are many other ways a Mage can accomplish his goals and always find a way around whatever. Just use alternatives instead of making up bizzare stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","user":"Bogdan","date":". 09-16-2016, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:36:33-07:00","id":970585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970578#post970578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 3 shadows should not take 3 times as much successes than 1 shadow, thats what additional targets are for.<br /> Chain-lighting is damage + targets not damage times targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. And while Revised was also a lot more strict and systematic with the success calculations, I think M20 has a good mindset of 'consider the overall total successes required for a feat of certain magnitude'.<br /> <br /> Needing over 90 successes to make a measly 3 strongish tentacles, while those 90 successes also allow you to nuke a chunk of a city, shows that the former really should require less based on 'what you get'. Else you run into both problems: Super effective, violent things requiring too few successes, and simple, mediocre things requiring too many, simply based on 'one single value increase for one success'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:42:52-07:00","id":970589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970584#post970584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, I don't think I get your point here.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Direct Damage effect charges only successes for damage once plus one additional success per target above one.<br /> <br /> Why should it be different for other effects? Why charge 15+15+15 for 3 shadows instead of 15+2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:48:44-07:00","id":970592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969924-obtenebration?p=970589#post970589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Direct Damage effect charges only successes for damage once plus one additional success per target above one.<br /> <br /> Why should it be different for other effects? Why charge 15+15+15 for 3 shadows instead of 15+2?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Already replied above with edit.<br /> <br /> Well, damage ain't other effects that's why lol. It's kind of obvious to me.<br /> <br /> Incinerate some person that pissed you off? That doesn't sound hard for a mage.<br /> <br /> Create three shadow tentacles of big power, big health, with their own mind and even possibly connected to you? Now that sounds like something you can't do just by snapping your fingers.<br /> <br /> But honestly, it's pointless to argue over that. I'm really following what books say, if you as Storyteller do not enjoy such ruleset - Golden Rule to the rescue. I prefer the book because it actually makes sense and balances the things out, disallowing mages to perform such complicated feats in a snap of finger (but allowing them to make it better than Vampires or Werewolves, for the cost of time and effort).<br /> <br /> Mage is all about excellence anyway, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:56:25-07:00","id":970597,"title":"","content":"All effects above 10 successes are beyond the scope of \u201cwith a snap of the fingers\u201c...<br /> <br /> Magick works different at every table, that is just fine. We all like to share our thoughts and opinions and try to convince others that we a